21-This story is the product's acceptance test. Full script with German lines and timings:
22-[research/pet-insurance/demo-video-script.md](research/pet-insurance/demo-video-script.md).
23-
24-**Mimi jumped off the wardrobe and is limping → 🟡 see a vet today → Pawse calls the vet in German → the insurer
25-confirms the accident is covered, but not the home visit or physio → the owner picks the clinic (about CHF 385
26-instead of 510) → Pawse confirms the vet, books a cat-friendly taxi, and hands over a case summary and claim checklist.**
27-
28-| Time | Beat | Backed by | Today |
29-|---|---|---|---|
30-| 0:00–0:17 | Owner records Mimi and says "My cat is limping" in English | `voice.py` transcription, `/care` intake | ✅ photo + audio via Gemini · ⚠️ video intake not connected |
31-| 0:17–0:30 | Triage card 🟡, follow-up "fall or jump?", nearest open practice | `providers.py` care guidance + clinic adapters, `orchestration.py` ranking | ✅ Gemini guidance · ✅ clinic search with phone numbers via Gemini Google Maps grounding (`GEMINI_API_KEY`), Places when configured, OSM snapshot fallback |
32-| 0:30–0:58 | German call to the vet: 16:30 or a home visit, ~CHF 600 + 150 | `voice.py` German script + subtitles, Gradium speech | ✅ script · ⚠️ own voice needs a Gradium key · 🎭 call and reply simulated (no telephony) |
33-| 0:58–1:30 | Insurer call: accident covered, home visit and physio not; clinic CHF 385 vs home CHF 510 | `knowledge.py` cited AVB clauses, `demo.py` cost maths, `research/pet-insurance/` | ✅ citations + maths (real AVB terms, synthetic policyholder) · 🎭 insurer reply simulated |
34-| 1:30–1:42 | Pawse confirms 16:30 with the vet, asks for an itemised invoice | `voice.py` script | ✅ script · 🎭 reply and booking simulated |
35-| 1:42–1:54 | Taxi for 16:05 that accepts a cat in a carrier | `voice.py` script | ✅ script · 🎭 reply and booking simulated |
36-| 1:54–2:00 | Case summary + claim checklist (keep video, itemised invoice, 30 days) | `demo.py`, frontend | ✅ |
37-
38-The in-app rehearsal (`GET /api/v1/demo/mimi`, first screen of the app) plays the whole story with no keys. It is the
39-fallback, not the goal.
40-
41-**Keep it really running.**
42-- The goal is the live path: each ⚠️ above is open work to turn into ✅ (or, if cut, an honest 🎭 label), not a footnote.
43-- Every change must leave the golden path working end to end. Before pushing anything that touches it, run
44-  `bash scripts/check.sh` and walk the story in the browser ([demo-check](.claude/skills/demo-check/SKILL.md)).

